{
  // Returned by describe_server — gives the agent an overview of available storage tools.
  "describe_server": "## Storage Service\n\nProvides access to the shared object store, organised per the ADR-007 folder layout.\n\n### Read-only exploration\nBrowse and read your company's files with `list_files`, `read_file`, `search_files`, `get_file_properties`, and `get_file_summary`. Paths start at your company folder (e.g. `knowledge/shared/`); the full keys these tools return work too. Call `describe_folder` with a path prefix to learn what a folder is for.\n\n### Your working directory (produce your outputs here)\nThe `*_working_file` tools act on your own assignment's working directory — you pass only a **filename** (subdirectories allowed); the location is derived from your assignment, so you cannot write outside it. Use `create_working_file` for a brand-new file or a full rewrite, `append_working_file` to add to a file, `replace_in_working_file` for a small in-place edit, `read_working_file`, `get_working_file_summary` (structure — headings/keys/CSV columns — without reading the whole file), `list_working_files`, and soft `delete_working_file`/`restore_working_file`. In qa mode these are read-only: you review the assignment under review, you do not modify it.\n\n### Your materials (your inputs)\nThe `*_material_file` tools expose the materials handed to your assignment — `list_material_files`, `read_material_file`, `get_material_file_properties`. Inline-text materials are read back as their literal content.\n\n### Company resources\nCompany resources are long-lived company documents such as invoices, price lists and policies. Use `list_resources`, `read_resource`, `write_resource`, `append_resource` and `replace_in_resource`, with paths like `invoices/INV-0042.md`. In a task your changes are drafts, applied to the company's resources when the task succeeds; in a chat they change the resources straight away.",

  // Folder descriptions returned by describe_folder, keyed by folder type.
  "describe_folder_task_materials": "**Task materials** — User-submitted inputs for this task (briefs, data files, reference documents). Read-only after task creation.",
  "describe_folder_task_completed": "**Task completed outputs** — The task's final deliverables, promoted from its assignments' `completed/` directories once every assignment succeeds. Accessible to all agents working the task.",
  "describe_folder_assignment_working": "**Assignment working area** — The private scratch area for one assignment's agent. Write intermediate results and final artefacts here before submitting via `complete_assignment`.",
  "describe_folder_assignment_completed": "**Assignment completed outputs** — Files promoted from an assignment's working area once QA accepts them. Later assignments and the task's finalisation step read from here.",
  "describe_folder_resources": "**Company resources** — Long-lived company documents (invoices, price lists, policies, listing copy). Read and change them with the resource tools (`list_resources`, `read_resource`, `write_resource`); each folder's `README.md` says what it is for.",
  "describe_folder_knowledge": "**Knowledge base** — OKF Markdown source documents for RAG indexing. Managed by the `store-knowledge` CLI command. Treat as read-only from within an agent.",
  "describe_folder_audit": "**Audit log** — Append-only JSONL audit entries written by the system. Do not modify.",
  "describe_folder_fallback": "No specific description is available for this path. Use `list_files` to explore its contents.",

